WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:03:08.650
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
03:08.920 --> 03:11.080
If I were a supervisor like you,

3
03:11.880 --> 03:14.040
I'd choose to protect my workers

4
03:14.120 --> 03:16.080
instead of criticizing me for what I did.

5
03:16.160 --> 03:17.080
PREVIOUSLY

6
03:17.160 --> 03:18.600
You're just a worker.

7
03:18.680 --> 03:20.200
What right do you have to lecture me?

8
03:20.280 --> 03:22.240
I thought you were a good supervisor.

9
03:22.320 --> 03:24.160
But now I know

10
03:24.240 --> 03:25.960
you're not as good as I thought.

11
03:26.040 --> 03:27.640
If you want anything to eat,

12
03:27.720 --> 03:29.440
I guess you'll have to make it yourself.

13
03:30.040 --> 03:34.080
But you need to finish all your work first.

14
03:34.160 --> 03:36.240
I don't trust Hathaya at all.

15
03:37.000 --> 03:40.800
I'm afraid Hathaya might try to hurt you.

16
03:40.880 --> 03:42.800
Where did you get that much money?

17
03:42.880 --> 03:44.520
I played cards all night

18
03:44.600 --> 03:47.000
and won another 300,000, Mom.

19
03:47.080 --> 03:50.200
So now we've got 800,000.

20
03:59.680 --> 04:03.600
I started with 500,000 and made 300,000 in just one night.

21
04:05.040 --> 04:08.080
If I take all 800,000 and play again,

22
04:08.160 --> 04:10.320
wouldn't I come back with more than a million?

23
04:16.200 --> 04:20.120
But what if I take all 800,000 and lose it?

24
04:21.959 --> 04:25.920
Who could possibly be that unlucky?

25
04:27.400 --> 04:30.120
No, no, 800,000 is already good enough.

26
04:35.160 --> 04:38.320
Have a seat and wait a moment. I'll make it for you right away.

27
04:53.560 --> 04:54.920
Mom is quite old

28
04:55.560 --> 04:56.880
and still has to stand and cook.

29
04:59.400 --> 05:03.160
How many plates to cook, how many years to work, just for a hundred grand?

30
05:08.480 --> 05:10.720
I already have plenty of capital.

31
05:11.440 --> 05:14.560
If I play one more night,

32
05:15.280 --> 05:17.120
I should be able to come back with a million.

33
05:27.040 --> 05:29.160
Hey! Why aren't you working?

34
05:29.240 --> 05:30.280
Sorry, boss.

35
05:31.000 --> 05:34.400
My hand hurts. My glove is torn.

36
05:34.480 --> 05:37.200
If your glove is torn, why didn't you buy a new one?

37
05:37.280 --> 05:39.880
Work as fast as I pay you.

38
05:43.200 --> 05:44.120
Where are you going?

39
05:44.200 --> 05:47.400
I'm giving him my gloves. I only carry stuff, so I don't need them.

40
05:47.480 --> 05:49.800
Stay out of it. Trust me.

41
05:52.000 --> 05:54.240
What are you standing there for? Get back to work!

42
05:54.320 --> 05:56.040
I was going to get my hard hat, boss.

43
05:56.120 --> 05:57.760
-Get your hard hat? -Yes.

44
05:57.840 --> 06:00.320
I told you to wear it this morning. Why did you take it off?

45
06:00.400 --> 06:02.040
Since you took it off, don't wear it.

46
06:02.120 --> 06:04.000
-Get back to work! -Sorry, boss.

47
06:05.240 --> 06:06.840
Oh, hey.

48
06:06.920 --> 06:10.000
All you care about is work. Don't you care about safety at all?

49
06:10.080 --> 06:12.400
What are you going to do if someone gets hurt?

50
06:12.480 --> 06:13.880
You're just a worker.

51
06:14.480 --> 06:16.160
Who are you to tell me how to do my job?

52
06:16.240 --> 06:19.080
Yes, I'm just your employee,

53
06:19.160 --> 06:21.400
but we still have the right to protect our own lives.

54
06:24.080 --> 06:26.360
And I'm warning you now

55
06:26.440 --> 06:30.000
because if there is an accident, you're the one who will be held responsible.

56
06:31.480 --> 06:34.400
I don't know what happened to you today,

57
06:34.480 --> 06:36.840
but you can't take your anger out on your workers.

58
06:36.920 --> 06:38.200
That's not acceptable.

59
06:40.480 --> 06:42.760
Honestly, I'm not worried about you,

60
06:42.840 --> 06:44.600
but this project belongs to Grandpa.

61
06:44.680 --> 06:46.200
I don't want to cause him any trouble.

62
06:56.640 --> 06:57.800
Hello.

63
06:59.720 --> 07:00.680
Damn it.

64
07:01.240 --> 07:03.120
-Max, watch the site. -Yes, boss.

65
07:03.960 --> 07:04.920
Yes.

66
07:05.000 --> 07:08.320
Everyone, keep working!

67
07:13.400 --> 07:17.200
DUANGJAI'S FOOD STALL

68
07:19.080 --> 07:20.440
Hathai.

69
07:21.640 --> 07:23.320
Hathai. Hathai.

70
07:24.000 --> 07:25.120
Hathai.

71
07:28.160 --> 07:31.120
Did she go gambling again?

72
07:31.200 --> 07:33.800
What am I going to do?

73
07:33.880 --> 07:36.640
Oh, Hathai! Good grief!

74
07:36.720 --> 07:38.400
What am I going to do?

75
07:40.000 --> 07:41.400
Mom!

76
07:41.480 --> 07:43.000
Why are you shouting?

77
07:43.080 --> 07:44.800
What's come over you?

78
07:44.880 --> 07:46.080
Where were you?

79
07:46.160 --> 07:48.200
Taking a shower.

80
07:48.280 --> 07:49.480
Where are you going now?

81
07:49.560 --> 07:52.680
I'm tired of listening to you nag me,

82
07:52.760 --> 07:55.360
so I'm going to pay those people back and get it over with.

83
07:56.800 --> 08:01.680
What a relief. You nearly gave me a heart attack just now.

84
08:01.760 --> 08:03.560
Thought you took the money to the den.

85
08:03.640 --> 08:07.280
At first, I was thinking about it.

86
08:07.360 --> 08:08.720
I…

87
08:08.800 --> 08:11.160
I felt sorry for you. I don't want to see you

88
08:11.240 --> 08:13.920
standing over that stove cooking all day.

89
08:14.000 --> 08:17.120
Then I thought about it again and got scared I'd lose everything.

90
08:18.320 --> 08:22.560
And I feel sorry for Hathaya too.

91
08:22.640 --> 08:25.160
I know she's not exactly

92
08:25.240 --> 08:27.560
living comfortably over there.

93
08:27.640 --> 08:30.000
I want her to come back and live here.

94
08:32.200 --> 08:34.880
I'm glad you think that way.

95
08:34.960 --> 08:38.200
Wait for me to take a quick shower. I'll go with you.

96
08:39.360 --> 08:40.400
Mom!

97
08:40.480 --> 08:43.480
This isn't a wedding or an ordination. What you're wearing is fine.

98
08:44.080 --> 08:45.160
Oh, really?

99
08:45.240 --> 08:47.920
Yeah. Then I'll put away the pork and vegetables first.

100
08:48.000 --> 08:50.480
-Yeah, yeah. -Go put everything away.

101
08:50.560 --> 08:51.720
I'll go get dressed.

102
08:58.200 --> 09:00.400
Aunt Duang, I need some boxed meals.

103
09:01.320 --> 09:04.880
I'm about to go run an errand. Order from the stall at the alley entrance.

104
09:04.960 --> 09:08.120
Come on. I came here specifically to support you.

105
09:08.200 --> 09:10.720
I need 30 boxes for the kids at the soccer field.

106
09:10.800 --> 09:14.320
-Thirty boxes? -Yes. Are you really turning that down?

107
09:15.400 --> 09:18.320
Mom. Go ahead and make the food. I'll go by myself.

108
09:19.120 --> 09:21.920
Come on. Don't worry.

109
09:22.000 --> 09:24.160
I've already made up my mind.

110
09:24.240 --> 09:26.480
If I break my word, may I--

111
09:26.560 --> 09:27.920
All right, all right.

112
09:28.440 --> 09:31.640
I trust you. Go and come straight back.

113
09:32.200 --> 09:34.360
Tonight, I'll order some barbecue for us.

114
09:34.960 --> 09:38.720
Sounds good, Mom. And put some of that barley tea

115
09:38.800 --> 09:41.840
in the fridge so it's ice cold. I'll be back soon.

116
09:41.920 --> 09:42.800
You little…

117
09:43.800 --> 09:46.360
-Have a seat and wait for your food. -Okay, Aunt Duang.

118
10:08.000 --> 10:10.320
Hey, Hathai.

119
10:10.400 --> 10:11.520
Hey, Jim.

120
10:11.600 --> 10:13.360
I heard

121
10:13.440 --> 10:15.840
you won big the other day, then you disappeared.

122
10:15.920 --> 10:18.680
Yeah. I won enough. I'm good.

123
10:18.760 --> 10:21.000
What's your zodiac sign?

124
10:21.600 --> 10:23.280
Leo. Why?

125
10:23.360 --> 10:25.400
Same as me!

126
10:25.480 --> 10:28.080
I just had my fortune read. They said

127
10:28.160 --> 10:31.920
Leos are on fire right now.

128
10:32.000 --> 10:35.200
Our luck is through the roof! Money's pouring in. I'm going back in

129
10:35.280 --> 10:37.080
to win another million or two.

130
10:37.160 --> 10:38.440
You coming?

131
10:39.280 --> 10:41.440
You go ahead.

132
10:41.520 --> 10:43.280
-Suit yourself. -Yeah.

133
10:58.760 --> 11:01.800
Hey! Make some room!

134
11:01.880 --> 11:04.520
The new millionaire is here!

135
11:04.600 --> 11:06.760
Come on! Deal the cards already.

136
11:07.320 --> 11:11.120
My luck is on fire.

137
11:11.200 --> 11:14.040
Come on!

138
11:26.840 --> 11:28.040
Excuse me.

139
11:28.960 --> 11:31.040
-Excuse me. -Yes?

140
11:31.120 --> 11:32.600
Do you work around here?

141
11:33.800 --> 11:34.760
Yes.

142
11:34.840 --> 11:38.120
I'm looking for someone who works on this project. Do you know him?

143
11:38.200 --> 11:40.080
Who are you looking for?

144
11:40.160 --> 11:42.720
His name is Ramil. I'm his father.

145
11:42.800 --> 11:43.920
Do you know him?

146
11:45.040 --> 11:46.760
Ramil is my supervisor.

147
11:50.800 --> 11:53.160
He is just up ahead.

148
11:53.240 --> 11:55.400
I'm sure he'll be happy to see his father.

149
11:58.840 --> 12:00.120
Why do you think

150
12:00.800 --> 12:02.760
he'll be happy to see me?

151
12:02.840 --> 12:06.280
This morning, Ramil seemed like something was bothering him.

152
12:06.360 --> 12:08.480
I don't know what happened.

153
12:08.560 --> 12:11.640
Maybe seeing his father will help him open up.

154
12:22.400 --> 12:23.400
What are you doing here?

155
12:23.480 --> 12:25.040
You're not supposed to be here.

156
12:34.400 --> 12:39.720
I know, but someone wants to see you. He came here looking for you.

157
12:41.240 --> 12:42.120
Who?

158
12:42.720 --> 12:43.920
Your father.

159
13:03.800 --> 13:05.880
Hathaya,

160
13:05.960 --> 13:07.320
who did you bring to the boss?

161
13:08.040 --> 13:09.760
Mr. Anon. Ramil's father.

162
13:44.720 --> 13:48.040
I've been trying to call you. You never answer my calls.

163
13:56.720 --> 13:59.080
I missed you, so I drove over to see you.

164
14:01.040 --> 14:02.680
Are you doing okay?

165
14:07.160 --> 14:10.360
That girl said something was bothering you today.

166
14:12.760 --> 14:14.880
If something's wrong, you can tell me.

167
14:15.720 --> 14:17.880
I can help you solve any problem.

168
14:29.640 --> 14:31.200
We haven't seen each other in months.

169
14:32.160 --> 14:33.000
Got a girlfriend?

170
14:36.040 --> 14:39.680
-Is there someone? I'll ask for her hand. -What do you want?

171
14:48.960 --> 14:50.040
I missed you.

172
14:51.080 --> 14:52.280
I wanted to see you.

173
14:55.280 --> 14:56.520
Miss me?

174
14:58.320 --> 15:00.040
Every time you call,

175
15:00.560 --> 15:01.800
it's always about some mess,

176
15:02.840 --> 15:04.400
some problem I have to fix.

177
15:07.120 --> 15:09.880
When are you going to stop bothering me?

178
15:10.480 --> 15:11.880
Ramil, I'm sorry.

179
15:13.200 --> 15:15.440
I never meant for everything to turn out that way.

180
15:15.520 --> 15:17.320
How many hundreds or thousands of times

181
15:18.840 --> 15:21.720
do I have to hear you say "I'm sorry" in my lifetime?

182
15:23.720 --> 15:26.040
Dad. Where are you going?

183
15:26.120 --> 15:27.400
I have to go work, son.

184
15:28.160 --> 15:32.120
One day, I'll come back for you. I'll buy you a big house.

185
15:32.880 --> 15:35.560
I don't want a house. I want to stay with you.

186
15:38.560 --> 15:39.480
‎I'm sorry.

187
15:40.920 --> 15:41.840
Dad.

188
15:44.080 --> 15:45.520
Stay with me, sweetheart.

189
15:46.520 --> 15:48.040
Let your father go.

190
15:56.880 --> 15:59.640
You're a coward. You ran away from your problems

191
16:00.320 --> 16:01.960
and left your wife and son to suffer.

192
16:02.040 --> 16:04.000
Take everything valuable.

193
16:08.400 --> 16:09.960
What are you doing?!

194
16:10.040 --> 16:12.760
Your husband owes my boss money. Where is he?

195
16:12.840 --> 16:15.520
He's gone. I don't know where he went.

196
16:16.280 --> 16:18.720
He skipped out on his debt. We're selling this stuff.

197
16:18.800 --> 16:21.880
No. Please don't.

198
16:21.960 --> 16:23.160
-Don't! -Don't hurt Mom!

199
16:23.240 --> 16:24.840
I won't give them to you!

200
16:24.920 --> 16:26.680
Hey, keep going.

201
16:27.640 --> 16:30.400
-No. -Damn it.

202
16:31.840 --> 16:33.360
Let's go.

203
16:33.440 --> 16:35.040
No!

204
16:35.680 --> 16:36.760
No!

205
16:41.000 --> 16:42.520
Dad! Dad's back!

206
16:50.200 --> 16:52.000
I know everything.

207
16:52.760 --> 16:54.040
I know what happened.

208
16:55.120 --> 16:58.560
Come live with me. I'll take care of you.

209
16:58.640 --> 17:00.000
Please.

210
17:06.000 --> 17:07.319
I had to live in that house

211
17:08.960 --> 17:10.960
like a servant.

212
17:12.400 --> 17:14.160
I had to be his son's playmate

213
17:15.000 --> 17:16.800
and tolerate their mistreatment.

214
17:17.680 --> 17:18.960
I endured all of it.

215
17:20.280 --> 17:21.280
Do you know why?

216
17:24.319 --> 17:27.760
Because I love Mom. I had to protect her.

217
17:28.720 --> 17:31.160
And what about you? Where were you?

218
17:32.000 --> 17:33.480
You ran away and saved yourself.

219
17:35.520 --> 17:36.960
You're selfish.

220
17:40.320 --> 17:42.040
I didn't mean for it to happen.

221
17:42.800 --> 17:44.960
I was deceived. I was cheated.

222
17:45.040 --> 17:47.120
I didn't know it was a Ponzi scheme.

223
17:48.520 --> 17:50.080
I'm sorry, son.

224
17:55.520 --> 18:00.240
But let's not talk about the past anymore. What's done is done.

225
18:02.720 --> 18:04.440
I won't hurt you again.

226
18:06.880 --> 18:08.160
I want to be with you…

227
18:11.680 --> 18:13.680
and make up for everything I did wrong.

228
18:39.560 --> 18:41.280
There's a business opportunity.

229
18:44.040 --> 18:47.360
It doesn't take much money to invest, but the profit is huge.

230
18:49.520 --> 18:51.560
I want to invest in it,

231
18:53.800 --> 18:55.280
but I don't have enough money.

232
19:00.800 --> 19:02.280
I just need to borrow it for a bit.

233
19:07.160 --> 19:09.720
Ramil, I promise I won't mess up this time.

234
19:12.400 --> 19:14.680
I'll pay you back every single baht,

235
19:14.760 --> 19:17.400
and I'll buy a huge house. Bigger than Saksit's.

236
19:20.480 --> 19:22.480
I only need to borrow 500,000.

237
19:26.480 --> 19:27.560
So in the end…

238
19:30.360 --> 19:31.760
it's about money.

239
19:44.640 --> 19:45.960
That's all I'm giving you.

240
19:52.320 --> 19:54.160
And let this be

241
19:55.280 --> 19:57.000
the last time.

242
19:58.960 --> 20:00.280
After this,

243
20:02.360 --> 20:03.800
don't come see me again.

244
20:08.720 --> 20:10.120
I won't bother you anymore.

245
20:11.440 --> 20:12.640
I won't ask for anything again.

246
20:15.920 --> 20:17.680
Go back to work.

247
20:41.720 --> 20:43.280
Goodbye, sir.

248
21:04.360 --> 21:05.880
Hathaya.

249
21:06.680 --> 21:07.520
I have to go.

250
21:12.320 --> 21:13.880
How dare you

251
21:14.720 --> 21:18.280
tell other people about my business? You even brought him here.

252
21:19.480 --> 21:22.680
You're talking about your father.

253
21:22.760 --> 21:24.280
None of your business.

254
21:26.000 --> 21:29.960
I saw that something was bothering you. I thought he might be able to help.

255
21:30.040 --> 21:33.680
If what I did upset you, I'm sorry.

256
21:34.360 --> 21:38.240
But you still shouldn't have spoken to him like that. He is your father.

257
21:39.000 --> 21:40.400
You must live

258
21:41.320 --> 21:42.760
in a pretty perfect world

259
21:44.400 --> 21:47.240
if you can imagine every family

260
21:47.320 --> 21:50.200
as a mother, father, and child

261
21:50.280 --> 21:51.600
hugging each other with love.

262
21:53.760 --> 21:54.800
You and I

263
21:56.200 --> 21:57.640
must be from different worlds.

264
21:58.560 --> 22:00.000
You don't know what it's like to only

265
22:01.400 --> 22:03.320
have a father when it's convenient for him.

266
22:07.360 --> 22:09.440
No matter how bad my life gets,

267
22:10.320 --> 22:12.440
I would never say something like that.

268
22:13.760 --> 22:18.000
Go. Get back to work. Go be a good person

269
22:19.400 --> 22:20.800
in your perfect fantasy world.

270
22:33.160 --> 22:36.520
Your life might actually be better than mine.

271
22:51.520 --> 22:53.680
HATHAI

272
22:55.520 --> 22:59.600
Hathai, did your battery die or something? Why can't I reach you?

273
23:14.440 --> 23:16.120
I've only got 500,000 left.

274
23:17.320 --> 23:19.040
I'd better stop now.

275
23:22.240 --> 23:24.200
Hey. Where are you going?

276
23:24.280 --> 23:28.040
Where's that Leo luck now? I'm down 300,000.

277
23:28.120 --> 23:30.880
Come on. You have to be patient.

278
23:30.960 --> 23:33.480
Leo has to fall before it rises.

279
23:33.560 --> 23:36.240
Then it shoots straight through the roof!

280
23:37.040 --> 23:38.920
Whatever. If you don't want to play, go home.

281
23:39.000 --> 23:40.200
I'm going in.

282
23:51.240 --> 23:52.880
Leo shoots to the top…

283
23:57.600 --> 23:59.320
Leo shoots to the top!

284
24:00.800 --> 24:03.240
Leo shoots to the top!

285
24:04.240 --> 24:06.880
Move!

286
24:06.960 --> 24:09.720
Leo is shooting to the top!

287
24:28.040 --> 24:31.320
Hathaya, that porridge smells so good. It looks delicious too.

288
24:32.000 --> 24:33.800
I made some for you too, Chaya.

289
24:35.480 --> 24:38.640
Thank you, my dearest big sister. You're the sweetest.

290
24:38.720 --> 24:42.440
So, how has it been working at the construction site?

291
24:44.720 --> 24:48.000
Oh no. Your hands are all rough.

292
24:48.080 --> 24:49.400
I can't accept this anymore.

293
24:49.480 --> 24:52.600
I'm going to talk to Grandpa and ask him to move you back into the office.

294
24:53.240 --> 24:54.200
Chaya!

295
24:55.160 --> 24:57.560
You don't have to. I can handle it.

296
24:57.640 --> 24:59.160
I don't want to bother Grandpa anymore.

297
25:00.960 --> 25:02.320
I feel sorry for you.

298
25:03.160 --> 25:05.560
If I get the chance, I'll talk to Grandpa

299
25:05.640 --> 25:06.960
and try to soften him up.

300
25:08.560 --> 25:10.560
Thank you so much, Chaya.

301
25:12.680 --> 25:15.000
And since you have to go to the construction site soon,

302
25:15.080 --> 25:17.520
I'll take the porridge to Grandpa for you.

303
25:18.880 --> 25:20.320
Thank you.

304
25:20.920 --> 25:22.680
Here.

305
25:22.760 --> 25:23.800
Alright.

306
25:31.680 --> 25:34.160
What is everyone doing? The food still isn't here.

307
25:34.240 --> 25:35.600
Exactly.

308
25:35.680 --> 25:37.760
Hathaya is completely useless.

309
25:37.840 --> 25:39.600
She knows

310
25:39.680 --> 25:42.320
you have to eat and take your medicine on time.

311
25:42.400 --> 25:44.200
I'll go deal with it.

312
25:45.000 --> 25:47.360
Hot rice porridge is ready.

313
25:52.520 --> 25:55.320
Where's Hathaya? Why are you carrying it yourself?

314
25:56.560 --> 25:58.720
The kitchen staff said Hathaya woke up late.

315
25:59.440 --> 26:00.840
I was worried about you, Grandpa,

316
26:00.920 --> 26:04.120
so I made you some rice porridge and prepared your medicine.

317
26:06.040 --> 26:07.360
How irresponsible can she be?

318
26:07.440 --> 26:11.200
If Chayanee hadn't gone into the kitchen to make this for you,

319
26:11.280 --> 26:14.000
you'd probably be starving by now.

320
26:14.640 --> 26:17.120
Mom, don't criticize Hathaya.

321
26:17.720 --> 26:21.080
She has to work at the construction site, so she must be exhausted.

322
26:22.280 --> 26:23.640
Grandpa, have some porridge.

323
26:29.080 --> 26:32.200
Does it need anything, Grandpa? I can adjust it next time.

324
26:32.800 --> 26:33.600
It's delicious, sweetheart.

325
26:34.800 --> 26:37.000
What about that marketing plan

326
26:37.080 --> 26:39.480
I asked you to do? Is it finished yet?

327
26:40.120 --> 26:41.840
I was away from home for several days

328
26:41.920 --> 26:44.640
because I was working on the marketing plan for you.

329
26:58.040 --> 26:58.880
Oh.

330
26:58.960 --> 27:00.200
Hathaya,

331
27:00.280 --> 27:02.120
you don't have to sit in the back today.

332
27:02.200 --> 27:04.240
Oh? Where's your boss?

333
27:04.320 --> 27:08.440
Boss is on a secret mission, so he sent me to pick you up.

334
27:08.520 --> 27:10.080
Oh.

335
27:10.160 --> 27:11.520
But

336
27:11.600 --> 27:15.320
if your boss finds out I'm in the front seat, you're in big trouble.

337
27:15.400 --> 27:17.080
Oh.

338
27:17.160 --> 27:20.600
If you don't say anything, and I don't say anything,

339
27:20.680 --> 27:21.760
no one will ever know.

340
27:21.840 --> 27:22.800
Come on. Get in.

341
27:26.640 --> 27:27.760
Let's go.

342
27:44.000 --> 27:45.280
RANONG PROVINCE

343
27:46.880 --> 27:49.280
I want to know who Hathaya's mother

344
27:49.360 --> 27:50.560
is living with

345
27:51.120 --> 27:52.040
and what she does

346
27:53.240 --> 27:55.560
and whether Hathaya's grandmother is really sick.

347
27:56.720 --> 28:00.160
I don't believe what Hathaya told me. I want the truth.

348
28:00.960 --> 28:03.800
According to the address on the ID card Mr. Pichai gave me,

349
28:04.880 --> 28:06.400
it should be somewhere around here.

350
28:17.680 --> 28:19.240
Don't think I'm being nosy,

351
28:19.800 --> 28:21.960
but what kind of secret mission is your boss on?

352
28:22.760 --> 28:24.640
To tell you the truth, I don't know either.

353
28:25.760 --> 28:28.320
All I know is Mr. Pichai asked him to help with something.

354
28:28.400 --> 28:30.920
Mr. Pichai is very kind to my boss.

355
28:31.000 --> 28:32.840
When something comes up, he calls him for help.

356
28:32.920 --> 28:35.000
What did Grandpa ask him to help with?

357
28:35.080 --> 28:36.120
Hit me!

358
28:36.200 --> 28:39.040
Come on, hit me! I said hit me!

359
28:39.120 --> 28:40.320
-Hit me! -Don't do this!

360
28:40.400 --> 28:41.440
Let go of me!

361
28:41.520 --> 28:43.720
-Let go of me! -Sir, calm down.

362
28:43.800 --> 28:44.960
What happened?

363
28:45.040 --> 28:47.360
Sir, please stop! You'll get others hurt, too.

364
28:47.440 --> 28:48.560
Let go of me!

365
28:48.640 --> 28:50.280
I have no other choice!

366
28:50.360 --> 28:51.960
Let go of me!

367
28:52.040 --> 28:54.920
-Come here. -Let go of me.

368
28:55.000 --> 28:57.000
-Let go of me. -Get out.

369
28:57.080 --> 28:59.080
Don't! Hey!

370
28:59.160 --> 29:01.040
Let go of my wife!

371
29:01.120 --> 29:02.720
Please calm down.

372
29:02.800 --> 29:05.640
You people need to stop and get out of my house!

373
29:05.720 --> 29:06.760
I'm going inside!

374
29:06.840 --> 29:09.240
You built your houses on public land.

375
29:09.320 --> 29:11.200
The Subdistrict Office is expanding the road.

376
29:11.280 --> 29:13.200
They sent several warning letters already.

377
29:13.280 --> 29:14.520
Time's up. The houses must go.

378
29:14.600 --> 29:16.320
We've lived here for decades!

379
29:16.400 --> 29:18.120
You can't just do this to us!

380
29:18.200 --> 29:19.520
That doesn't change anything.

381
29:19.600 --> 29:23.040
This is public land. What you're doing is illegal.

382
29:23.120 --> 29:24.800
But the previous Chief

383
29:24.880 --> 29:27.600
allowed us to live here, and now all of a sudden

384
29:27.680 --> 29:30.280
you people are trying to throw us out? That's unacceptable.

385
29:30.360 --> 29:32.520
The houses come down, like it or not. Just doing our job.

386
29:33.120 --> 29:35.480
-If you tear it down, I'll kill you! -Yeah!

387
29:35.560 --> 29:37.440
-Go away. -Get out!

388
29:37.520 --> 29:41.000
-Back off! -You're dead!

389
29:41.080 --> 29:43.640
-Go away. -Get out!

390
29:43.720 --> 29:45.560
Stop. Stop!

391
29:45.640 --> 29:46.960
Enough! Please stop!

392
29:47.040 --> 29:48.560
Stop! Enough.

393
29:48.640 --> 29:51.240
Please stop!

394
29:51.320 --> 29:52.640
This has nothing to do with you.

395
29:52.720 --> 29:53.920
How does this not involve me?

396
29:54.000 --> 29:56.640
You drove him to jump in front of a car!

397
29:56.720 --> 29:59.040
I nearly killed someone because of this problem.

398
29:59.120 --> 30:01.520
It's over now. You can leave.

399
30:01.600 --> 30:03.280
You really think you can handle this?

400
30:07.160 --> 30:09.240
I don't think this is going to end easily.

401
30:09.960 --> 30:12.240
Let me step in and help both sides talk this through.

402
30:13.720 --> 30:14.680
Everyone.

403
30:17.080 --> 30:18.920
My name is Hathaya.

404
30:19.000 --> 30:22.520
I have no personal interest in this matter.

405
30:22.600 --> 30:24.960
I just want to act as a mediator and help both sides

406
30:25.040 --> 30:26.240
talk through the problem.

407
30:26.320 --> 30:27.160
Oh.

408
30:27.240 --> 30:30.720
Please help us. We're being treated unfairly.

409
30:31.360 --> 30:32.200
Please.

410
30:32.280 --> 30:33.480
Please help us.

411
30:51.680 --> 30:52.800
Grandpa,

412
30:52.880 --> 30:54.800
come into the office first.

413
30:54.880 --> 30:57.400
I'm going to present my PR and marketing plans.

414
30:57.480 --> 31:01.200
I guarantee you're going to be impressed.

415
31:02.440 --> 31:03.440
Let's go.

416
31:06.840 --> 31:09.640
The Subdistrict Office sent written notices according to procedure.

417
31:09.720 --> 31:11.320
The residents were informed.

418
31:11.400 --> 31:13.320
Now that time's up, they're resisting us.

419
31:13.400 --> 31:16.360
That's a lie! You just showed up and started tearing everything down.

420
31:16.440 --> 31:18.120
The evidence is right here.

421
31:18.200 --> 31:20.480
The dates are clear. They got a month's notice.

422
31:20.560 --> 31:22.680
Don't believe them.

423
31:22.760 --> 31:24.480
We never received

424
31:24.560 --> 31:26.440
any warning letters.

425
31:26.520 --> 31:27.920
We only came here

426
31:28.000 --> 31:29.800
after hearing they're demolishing our homes!

427
31:29.880 --> 31:31.920
-That's why all of us came to protest. -Yes.

428
31:32.000 --> 31:34.680
-Yes. -We've lived here for so long.

429
31:34.760 --> 31:37.360
If it's really illegal, why wait until now to evict us?

430
31:37.440 --> 31:39.000
-Right, everyone? -Yes.

431
31:39.080 --> 31:40.120
That's right.

432
31:40.200 --> 31:41.640
Why didn't they make us leave before?

433
31:41.720 --> 31:43.240
You said you were going to help us.

434
31:43.320 --> 31:44.760
Then tell them

435
31:44.840 --> 31:46.080
they can't just throw us out.

436
31:46.160 --> 31:48.160
-Right, everyone? -Yes.

437
31:48.240 --> 31:50.280
Tell them!

438
31:50.360 --> 31:52.320
Everyone, please listen.

439
31:53.080 --> 31:55.120
From what I can see in these documents,

440
31:55.200 --> 31:57.240
this land is public property.

441
31:57.320 --> 31:59.200
Homes cannot legally be built here.

442
31:59.280 --> 32:01.560
You work for the Subdistrict Office, don't you?!

443
32:01.640 --> 32:03.720
Get out! Get out!

444
32:03.800 --> 32:06.920
Get out! Get out!

445
32:07.000 --> 32:08.680
Get out! Get out!

446
32:08.760 --> 32:10.680
Please listen to me first!

447
32:13.560 --> 32:15.080
Listen!

448
32:15.160 --> 32:18.000
I have nothing to gain from either side.

449
32:18.080 --> 32:19.440
I'm only trying to help.

450
32:21.360 --> 32:23.240
I've been evicted plenty of times myself.

451
32:24.800 --> 32:26.440
My situation isn't that different.

452
32:31.320 --> 32:32.640
I really do want to help.

453
32:50.960 --> 32:52.040
Excuse me.

454
32:53.520 --> 32:55.160
Do you know

455
32:56.240 --> 32:57.600
where this person lives?

456
32:58.320 --> 32:59.360
No.

457
33:15.760 --> 33:16.720
Excuse me.

458
33:18.440 --> 33:20.600
Do you know this person?

459
33:22.680 --> 33:23.680
No.

460
33:25.760 --> 33:26.760
Thank you.

461
33:29.600 --> 33:31.360
My life has been difficult too.

462
33:31.440 --> 33:32.280
NO DEMOLITION!

463
33:32.360 --> 33:34.200
I understand what you're going through.

464
33:34.880 --> 33:36.160
Please let me help.

465
33:36.800 --> 33:38.240
Then what are we supposed to do?

466
33:38.320 --> 33:41.320
The houses were built illegally. You have to move.

467
33:41.400 --> 33:42.880
Officer,

468
33:43.400 --> 33:44.920
you only care about tearing down homes.

469
33:45.000 --> 33:46.640
Don't you feel any sympathy for them?

470
33:47.200 --> 33:48.880
Your salary

471
33:48.960 --> 33:51.280
comes from taxpayers.

472
33:51.360 --> 33:53.680
If you're going to talk to people like that, think first.

473
33:54.800 --> 33:57.520
You should be helping them find a solution.

474
33:57.600 --> 33:59.840
Don't take our taxes and then leave people homeless.

475
34:00.480 --> 34:01.600
Hey.

476
34:01.680 --> 34:03.000
I like what she's saying!

477
34:03.080 --> 34:05.240
She's on our side!

478
34:06.760 --> 34:08.320
-Applause. -Yeah!

479
34:08.400 --> 34:10.000
Here.

480
34:10.080 --> 34:12.080
Let's film this.

481
34:12.159 --> 34:13.560
People online need to see

482
34:13.639 --> 34:16.280
what these officials are doing to us.

483
34:16.360 --> 34:18.000
-Right?! -Right.

484
34:18.080 --> 34:21.840
If you want to demolish their homes, then you have to answer one question.

485
34:21.920 --> 34:24.000
Once you force them out, where will they go?

486
34:27.000 --> 34:28.920
Hello, everyone.

487
34:29.000 --> 34:30.000
Hello.

488
34:30.080 --> 34:32.040
Hello, everyone.

489
34:32.600 --> 34:35.960
Our Subdistrict Office has not ignored this issue.

490
34:36.040 --> 34:39.159
We've already prepared a complete relocation plan.

491
34:39.880 --> 34:42.960
And most importantly, as the Chief here,

492
34:43.040 --> 34:44.520
I can assure you that

493
34:44.600 --> 34:47.159
once you move out, you will definitely have somewhere to live.

494
34:47.239 --> 34:48.239
We don't want it!

495
34:48.320 --> 34:50.639
It's far away and as quiet as a graveyard.

496
34:50.719 --> 34:52.400
How are we supposed to make a living?

497
34:54.960 --> 34:56.360
Well…

498
34:56.440 --> 34:59.760
It may be quiet now, but I believe that once all of you

499
34:59.840 --> 35:00.760
build homes there,

500
35:00.840 --> 35:04.120
and it becomes a larger community, it won't be quiet anymore.

501
35:04.200 --> 35:05.120
Moreover,

502
35:05.200 --> 35:07.120
most of your neighbors

503
35:07.200 --> 35:08.600
have already moved out.

504
35:08.680 --> 35:12.160
We're asking everyone in this community to cooperate

505
35:12.240 --> 35:15.720
for the sake of development and the greater good.

506
35:17.000 --> 35:18.000
Chief,

507
35:18.960 --> 35:22.120
I agree with development and considering the greater good.

508
35:22.800 --> 35:26.920
But I don't agree with using the majority as an excuse to ignore the minority.

509
35:28.520 --> 35:31.920
True democracy isn't just about listening to the majority.

510
35:32.520 --> 35:34.480
It also means listening to the minority.

511
35:34.560 --> 35:38.160
The majority should not be used to pressure the minority into silence.

512
35:39.480 --> 35:41.320
We need to work together to solve this.

513
35:41.400 --> 35:44.720
We need to find the fairest solution.

514
35:46.400 --> 35:49.880
You know these houses are illegal.

515
35:50.560 --> 35:53.200
Yes. The evidence is clear.

516
35:53.760 --> 35:55.560
Everyone knows the houses are illegal.

517
35:58.360 --> 36:00.360
But you can't blame the residents alone.

518
36:00.880 --> 36:02.640
Officials neglected the situation

519
36:03.280 --> 36:05.920
and allowed them to live here illegally for decades.

520
36:06.600 --> 36:08.280
That means the authorities

521
36:09.040 --> 36:11.800
failed in their duty too. Right?

522
36:11.880 --> 36:13.360
-That's right. -That's right.

523
36:13.440 --> 36:14.680
The officials are at fault too.

524
36:14.760 --> 36:18.680
If the authorities had done their jobs properly

525
36:18.760 --> 36:20.160
and fairly from the beginning,

526
36:20.240 --> 36:22.880
this problem would never have reached this point.

527
36:23.520 --> 36:26.040
I don't want to place all the blame on the villagers.

528
36:27.520 --> 36:29.520
The authorities need to examine their actions

529
36:29.600 --> 36:32.200
and accept accountability for their part in this too.

530
36:33.240 --> 36:36.320
-Yes! -That's right!

531
36:36.400 --> 36:37.760
-True. -Take responsibility.

532
36:37.840 --> 36:40.360
And from what I've heard,

533
36:40.440 --> 36:43.640
they're angry because the office is rushing to tear down their homes.

534
36:44.520 --> 36:46.280
If they're relocated far away,

535
36:46.360 --> 36:48.480
how are their children supposed to get to school?

536
36:48.560 --> 36:49.440
Where will they study?

537
36:49.520 --> 36:51.680
How are they supposed to earn a living?

538
36:51.760 --> 36:53.080
Where will they make money?

539
36:53.160 --> 36:54.720
If they can't make a living,

540
36:54.800 --> 36:57.360
they'll just have to pack up their children and belongings

541
36:57.440 --> 36:59.560
and build another shack

542
36:59.640 --> 37:01.600
along a road or canal.

543
37:01.680 --> 37:03.760
Their lives will keep going in the same cycle.

544
37:06.960 --> 37:10.640
I understand the need for development and expanding the road.

545
37:11.240 --> 37:13.280
And I know allocating land to the villagers

546
37:13.360 --> 37:14.920
would be difficult

547
37:15.000 --> 37:16.560
since land here is costly.

548
37:17.760 --> 37:19.120
Exactly.

549
37:20.080 --> 37:23.240
Since you understand that, and everyone else understands it too,

550
37:23.320 --> 37:27.200
then we should all be moving in the same direction.

551
37:27.280 --> 37:29.760
Please cooperate with the plan we've already prepared.

552
37:36.360 --> 37:39.600
I won't let you keep living a wandering life like this.

553
37:42.720 --> 37:46.080
I'll do my best to make sure you can still earn a living around here.

554
37:50.120 --> 37:51.880
Thank you very much.

555
38:14.520 --> 38:17.800
This is the marketing plan I'm very proud to present to you, Grandpa.

556
38:17.880 --> 38:21.440
I want to begin by promoting our housing development through a campaign.

557
38:21.520 --> 38:23.440
We'll hire a famous actor

558
38:23.520 --> 38:26.000
as the face of the project.

559
38:26.080 --> 38:29.160
It'll make our development the talk of the town.

560
38:37.840 --> 38:40.560
We're not a large company.

561
38:40.640 --> 38:42.640
We don't need to spend that much money.

562
38:44.560 --> 38:49.400
I want our brand to become a national brand.

563
38:50.000 --> 38:52.840
Then, eventually, we can take the company public.

564
38:52.920 --> 38:54.880
I'm not thinking only about today.

565
38:54.960 --> 38:57.680
I want us to look toward the future, Grandpa.

566
38:59.920 --> 39:02.400
I agree with Chayanee.

567
39:02.480 --> 39:05.040
These days, you can't stay small

568
39:05.120 --> 39:06.760
and operate like a family business forever.

569
39:06.840 --> 39:10.120
We need to grow into a major national company.

570
39:12.160 --> 39:13.800
I put a lot of thought

571
39:13.880 --> 39:16.920
and effort into this for our family.

572
39:35.040 --> 39:38.680
Next time, don't make me come down here and fix a problem like this myself.

573
39:39.200 --> 39:40.840
If this happens again,

574
39:40.920 --> 39:42.480
you're all fired.

575
39:43.080 --> 39:44.400
I'm sorry, Chief.

576
39:44.480 --> 39:45.440
Go!

577
39:48.400 --> 39:49.480
Oh.

578
39:50.480 --> 39:52.200
By the way, that young woman…

579
39:52.960 --> 39:54.760
Is she related to someone around here?

580
39:54.840 --> 39:56.040
No, Dad.

581
39:56.720 --> 39:59.280
That woman is Mr. Pichai's eldest granddaughter.

582
40:00.320 --> 40:02.080
Oh!

583
40:03.040 --> 40:04.680
Mr. Pichai's granddaughter.

584
40:06.400 --> 40:09.600
No wonder she's so full of herself and thinks she knows everything.

585
40:09.680 --> 40:11.160
I'd like to see whether

586
40:11.240 --> 40:13.360
she can actually deliver

587
40:14.040 --> 40:15.400
on what she promised them

588
40:16.640 --> 40:18.440
or whether she's all talk.

589
40:25.720 --> 40:27.080
I helped mediate

590
40:27.160 --> 40:31.120
until the Subdistrict Office agreed to give people more time.

591
40:32.880 --> 40:34.320
What does that have to do with me?

592
40:34.400 --> 40:35.560
Exactly.

593
40:35.640 --> 40:38.840
The Subdistrict Office is demolishing illegal homes. Everything is legal.

594
40:38.920 --> 40:40.760
That's the end of it.

595
40:40.840 --> 40:43.440
You shouldn't be interfering.

596
40:43.520 --> 40:45.080
Go back to work.

597
40:45.680 --> 40:48.080
I came to ask for your kindness, Grandpa.

598
40:48.960 --> 40:50.240
Hey.

599
40:50.320 --> 40:52.240
I told you to go back to work. Are you deaf?

600
40:53.840 --> 40:56.840
The villagers are in trouble. I think you can help them, Grandpa.

601
40:56.920 --> 40:58.320
Enough of your nonsense.

602
40:58.400 --> 40:59.320
Go!

603
41:00.360 --> 41:01.520
What do you want?

604
41:03.400 --> 41:06.160
I noticed there's an empty area behind the project.

605
41:06.240 --> 41:08.040
It hasn't been used for anything.

606
41:17.800 --> 41:20.240
I think if we let the villagers stay there,

607
41:20.320 --> 41:21.880
we can help them.

608
41:23.880 --> 41:26.400
Do you think our company is some kind of charity?

609
41:27.680 --> 41:29.080
Absolutely not, Father.

610
41:29.160 --> 41:31.440
We can't let those people live there.

611
41:32.120 --> 41:35.160
They know how to manipulate the system and take advantage.

612
41:35.240 --> 41:38.080
If they stay long enough, they'll try to claim ownership.

613
41:40.960 --> 41:43.240
They would stay there as our workers.

614
41:46.800 --> 41:49.160
Most of them already work as day laborers.

615
41:49.240 --> 41:51.160
We can hire them to work for us.

616
41:51.240 --> 41:54.520
Our development is being rushed, and we need more workers.

617
41:55.120 --> 41:56.280
Hathaya,

618
41:57.000 --> 41:58.880
once the project is finished,

619
41:58.960 --> 42:00.400
they'll be unemployed again.

620
42:00.480 --> 42:04.360
Once construction finishes, property management will still need cleaners.

621
42:04.440 --> 42:07.560
and security guards. These people are locals.

622
42:07.640 --> 42:09.440
I believe they could be a great help to us.

623
42:09.520 --> 42:11.200
Now you've completely lost your mind.

624
42:11.880 --> 42:13.400
I disagree, Father.

625
42:13.480 --> 42:15.760
Those people drink, use drugs,

626
42:15.840 --> 42:18.520
and constantly cause trouble.

627
42:22.280 --> 42:24.960
The villagers who are being evicted came to see Mr. Pichai.

628
42:25.040 --> 42:27.680
You brought them here to pressure Father, didn't you?

629
42:27.760 --> 42:29.040
No.

630
42:30.440 --> 42:33.360
I know my words alone may not be convincing.

631
42:34.040 --> 42:35.720
I wanted you to see them for yourself

632
42:35.800 --> 42:39.360
and understand how they feel,

633
42:39.440 --> 42:42.840
but whether you agree or refuse

634
42:43.600 --> 42:45.840
is entirely your decision, Grandpa.

635
42:45.920 --> 42:49.280
Father, don't go out there. I'll go chase them away myself.

636
42:50.080 --> 42:51.480
If they refuse to leave,

637
42:51.560 --> 42:54.440
-I'll call the cops to drag them out! -Grandpa.

638
42:54.520 --> 42:55.720
Grandpa.

639
43:04.440 --> 43:06.360
Sir, please.

640
43:06.440 --> 43:08.560
Sir, I want to work.

641
43:08.640 --> 43:11.960
-Sir, I want to work. -We want to work.

642
43:12.040 --> 43:13.920
-Please. -Everyone, please.

643
43:14.000 --> 43:15.120
-Calm down. -Calm down.

644
43:15.200 --> 43:16.640
Please, calm down first.

645
43:17.160 --> 43:18.240
Sir,

646
43:18.800 --> 43:21.040
please let us stay here too.

647
43:21.120 --> 43:22.880
Please, sir.

648
43:22.960 --> 43:24.760
Sir, I swear

649
43:24.840 --> 43:27.400
I'll work as hard as I can.

650
43:27.480 --> 43:28.640
Please.

651
43:29.960 --> 43:32.000
Father, don't give in.

652
43:32.080 --> 43:33.440
Listen to me.

653
43:34.160 --> 43:35.920
If you hire these people,

654
43:36.000 --> 43:37.840
sooner or later, they'll cause trouble.

655
43:38.640 --> 43:41.600
And if they damage the project, who's going to take responsibility?!

656
43:41.680 --> 43:43.320
I will.

657
43:43.840 --> 43:45.520
If anything goes wrong,

658
43:45.600 --> 43:47.160
I'll go home immediately,

659
43:47.240 --> 43:49.320
and I'll never bother you again.

660
43:53.040 --> 43:56.400
They're not your relatives. You don't know them.

661
43:57.320 --> 44:00.840
What were you thinking, risking your own life for them?

662
44:02.480 --> 44:04.200
Not everyone gets equal opportunities.

663
44:04.840 --> 44:06.400
I want to give them one.

664
44:18.400 --> 44:19.520
All right. Go.

665
44:20.640 --> 44:22.040
You can all go home now.

666
44:28.040 --> 44:30.440
Go pack up all your belongings.

667
44:31.800 --> 44:33.520
Then come back here and work for me.

668
44:34.160 --> 44:35.320
Build houses for me.

669
44:40.960 --> 44:43.240
Thank you so much, sir.

670
44:43.320 --> 44:45.160
We'll never forget your kindness.

671
44:45.240 --> 44:47.280
All right.

672
44:47.360 --> 44:48.960
Get up. There's no need to cry.

673
44:50.680 --> 44:52.520
I only ask one thing.

674
44:53.040 --> 44:55.200
Work hard and do your best.

675
44:55.800 --> 44:58.480
You've been given a good opportunity. Don't waste it.

676
45:06.640 --> 45:07.840
Yay!

677
45:07.920 --> 45:09.760
We have jobs now!

678
45:09.840 --> 45:11.120
Thank you so much.

679
45:11.200 --> 45:14.200
-Thank you! -Congrats.

680
45:14.280 --> 45:15.880
I'm so happy.

681
45:15.960 --> 45:17.560
Thank you.

682
45:17.640 --> 45:19.280
We're hired!

683
45:20.080 --> 45:22.960
I worked so hard on that marketing plan to impress Grandpa,

684
45:24.000 --> 45:26.920
but Hathaya stole the spotlight and grabbed all his attention.

685
45:27.000 --> 45:28.280
I hate her.

686
45:29.480 --> 45:32.760
Sweetheart, I warned you not to underestimate her.

687
45:32.840 --> 45:36.280
She came back here to steal our inheritance,

688
45:36.360 --> 45:39.880
and she's bringing in a whole group of parasites to support her.

689
45:39.960 --> 45:43.360
Next, she'll take everything.

690
45:44.920 --> 45:47.640
I won't let her take what belongs to me.

691
45:48.400 --> 45:50.520
I'll get rid of these parasites myself!

692
46:13.000 --> 46:15.120
Hathaya asked Mr. Pichai for work

693
46:16.120 --> 46:17.880
to pay for her grandma's treatment?

694
46:21.680 --> 46:23.120
She looks perfectly healthy.

695
46:24.480 --> 46:25.600
Hathaya

696
46:26.200 --> 46:27.680
really did make the whole thing up.

697
46:28.200 --> 46:31.880
DUANGJAI'S FOOD STALL

698
46:32.800 --> 46:35.800
What are you thinking about? You've been staring at me for a while.

699
46:36.840 --> 46:37.680
Oh!

700
46:37.760 --> 46:40.880
I was just thinking your cooking must be delicious.

701
46:40.960 --> 46:43.080
It smells amazing.

702
46:43.160 --> 46:47.200
Spicy pork basil with a runny fried egg, just like you ordered.

703
46:49.320 --> 46:51.280
That looks great.

704
46:56.320 --> 46:57.840
Don't forget this.

705
46:57.920 --> 46:59.680
You really know what I like.

706
47:00.280 --> 47:02.160
A fried egg needs chilies like this.

707
47:02.760 --> 47:06.760
That's how I like it too. But I'm old. My granddaughter won't let me have it.

708
47:06.840 --> 47:08.080
She fears for my kidneys.

709
47:09.960 --> 47:10.920
Well,

710
47:11.600 --> 47:12.840
is your granddaughter not here?

711
47:14.360 --> 47:16.560
No. She went to Pathum Thani.

712
47:18.640 --> 47:20.200
What is she doing there?

713
47:23.320 --> 47:26.000
I don't want to talk about it. It makes me angry.

714
47:28.520 --> 47:30.720
Sounds like this granddaughter of yours

715
47:30.800 --> 47:34.200
causes you a lot of trouble.

716
47:35.680 --> 47:37.520
If I could turn back time,

717
47:37.600 --> 47:39.560
I never would've let her go.

718
47:40.120 --> 47:42.880
Did your granddaughter go cause trouble

719
47:43.600 --> 47:45.200
or deceive someone?

720
47:45.800 --> 47:48.080
My granddaughter has never deceived anyone.

721
47:48.160 --> 47:49.440
She's a good person!

722
47:50.320 --> 47:51.280
A good person.

723
47:51.360 --> 47:53.320
Of course she is.

724
47:53.400 --> 47:57.080
When I said someone deceived us and caused us pain,

725
47:57.160 --> 47:58.760
I was talking about someone else.

726
47:59.800 --> 48:02.720
My granddaughter is as good as an angel.

727
48:07.520 --> 48:12.600
Why do you keep asking about my granddaughter? What are you thinking?

728
48:12.680 --> 48:13.760
Are you after her?

729
48:13.840 --> 48:15.560
Grandma,

730
48:16.120 --> 48:18.960
of course not. I'm not from around here.

731
48:19.040 --> 48:20.920
I don't even know your granddaughter.

732
48:21.560 --> 48:25.400
What were you going to tell me? What's she doing out in Pathum Thani?

733
48:27.040 --> 48:28.120
It's a long story.

734
48:29.520 --> 48:31.880
That's okay. I'm not in a hurry.

735
48:31.960 --> 48:34.040
If there's anything you want to tell me,

736
48:34.120 --> 48:35.920
I'm listening.

737
48:54.760 --> 48:55.840
Hey!

738
48:55.920 --> 48:57.360
Why are you setting those off?

739
48:58.040 --> 48:59.600
If something happens to her,

740
48:59.680 --> 49:00.720
you're going to jail!

741
49:00.800 --> 49:02.400
This has nothing to do with you.

742
49:02.480 --> 49:03.400
Stay out of it.

743
49:03.480 --> 49:04.600
Where's your daughter?

744
49:04.680 --> 49:07.320
Hathai took the money to pay you.

745
49:09.600 --> 49:11.360
Listen to this old lady.

746
49:11.440 --> 49:13.440
She says her daughter brought us the money.

747
49:14.920 --> 49:17.080
-She did! -If she paid her debt,

748
49:17.160 --> 49:18.840
I wouldn't even be here!

749
49:18.920 --> 49:21.760
I'm telling the truth. She left with the money yesterday.

750
49:21.840 --> 49:23.520
She still hasn't come back.

751
49:23.600 --> 49:24.920
She hasn't paid us anything.

752
49:25.000 --> 49:26.960
You people are trying to mess with us?

753
49:34.240 --> 49:35.680
Hey.

754
49:37.400 --> 49:39.680
And now we don't have any money left to pay the debt.

755
49:39.760 --> 49:41.000
What are we going to do?

756
49:41.080 --> 49:42.400
Mom, call Hathaya.

757
49:42.480 --> 49:44.280
Hathaya listens to you.

758
49:44.360 --> 49:47.320
If she doesn't have the money, she'll find a way. Please, Mom.

759
49:47.400 --> 49:49.160
If any problem comes up,

760
49:49.240 --> 49:50.640
you have to leave this house.

761
49:50.720 --> 49:52.760
If you like Hathaya so much,

762
49:52.840 --> 49:54.360
then go see her.

763
49:54.440 --> 49:56.200
I don't have feelings for your cousin.

764
49:56.280 --> 49:57.920
Then why are you getting involved with her?

765
49:58.000 --> 49:59.040
NEXT EPISODE

766
49:59.120 --> 50:00.200
I hate her.

767
50:00.280 --> 50:02.680
You're the Chief. You should be at the Subdistrict Office.

768
50:02.760 --> 50:05.080
Don't go around courting businesspeople

769
50:05.160 --> 50:06.520
for your own benefit.

770
52:00.840 --> 52:02.800
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
